    "from_line": 239,
    "to_line": 253,
    "why": "The KeepAlive component's onBeforeUnmount handler walks every cached branch and decides its fate: the branch matching the current subtree has its keep-alive shape flag reset and deactivated hooks queued (so it is kept/detached and unmounts with KeepAlive), while every other cached branch is unmounted outright."
  },
  {
    "path": "packages/runtime-vapor/src/components/KeepAlive.ts",
    "from_line": 336,
    "to_line": 372,
    "why": "The Vapor KeepAlive onBeforeUnmount handler makes the same decision for cached branches — unset shape flags and fire deactivated hooks for the current entry (kept/detached) versus remove() for all other cached branches (removed outright), plus a fallback for a live current block not yet stored in cache."
  },
  {
    "path": "packages/runtime-core/src/renderer.ts",
    "from_line": 2413,
    "to_line": 2424,
    "why": "In the generic unmount path, a component vnode whose shapeFlag has COMPONENT_SHOULD_KEEP_ALIVE is detoured into the KeepAlive context's deactivate() (moved to the storage container, i.e. detached) instead of being torn down, which is the single-vnode-level decision between detached and removed."
  },
  {
    "path": "packages/runtime-vapor/src/component.ts",
    "from_line": 1280,
    "to_line": 1295,
    "why": "Vapor's unmountComponent skips real unmount for a kept-alive component (COMPONENT_SHOULD_KEEP_ALIVE set) and instead calls the parent KeepAlive ctx.deactivate() to detach it, otherwise falling through to a full removal."
  },
  {
    "path": "packages/runtime-core/src/components/KeepAlive.ts",
    "from_line": 189,
    "to_line": 200,
    "why": "pruneCacheEntry decides, when a cached branch is pruned (include/exclude/max), whether to unmount the cached branch outright or, if it is the current active one, merely reset its keep-alive flags so it will be unmounted later."
  },
  {
    "path": "packages/runtime-core/src/components/KeepAlive.ts",
    "from_line": 168,
    "to_line": 172,
    "why": "The unmount helper strips the keep-alive shape flags via resetShapeFlag and then calls the real renderer unmount, which is what executes the 'removed outright' path for cached branches."
  }
]
